    {
      "id": "lv-28",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -800,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 1000,
        "color": 1,
        "content": "## Long video to captioned vertical clips, posted on a schedule\n\n**Who it's for:** podcasters, coaches, educators and marketing teams who record long videos and want a week of Shorts, Reels and TikToks out of each one, without an editor.\n\n**What it does:** you drop a video (file or link) into a form. **Rendley** transcribes it, OpenAI picks the strongest self-contained moments and writes a caption for each, and the **Rendley AI video agent** turns every moment into a vertical clip: cut to the moment, reframed to 9:16 so the speaker stays in frame, filler words removed, word-by-word captions. Rendley exports each clip and posts it to the accounts you connected (TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, X, LinkedIn and more), one clip at a time on the schedule you set.\n\n**Review built in:** every post waits in the Rendley content calendar until its time, so you can watch it, edit the project, reschedule or cancel.\n\n### Set up (about 5 minutes)\n1. In app.rendley.com connect your social accounts under **Social media** and create an API key (paid plan).\n2. Add credentials for Rendley and OpenAI. Pick your accounts in **Post the clip**.\n3. Adjust **Settings**, activate the workflow and open the form URL from **On form submission**.\n\n### Requirements\nRendley paid plan with credits and social publishing, OpenAI API key. One video with speech, up to the length your Rendley plan imports.\n\n### Customize\nNumber and length of clips, aspect ratio, caption look and the posting schedule live in **Settings**. What makes a good moment is in **Pick the best moments**. Set **postPartialClips** to true to also post clips the agent finished with warnings."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lv-29",
      "name": "Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1640,
        "height": 560,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "### 1. The video comes in\nThe form takes a file or a public link. Rendley stores it in a new project, so the original stays in your library."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lv-30",
      "name": "Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1620,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1060,
        "height": 640,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "### 2. Find the moments\nRendley transcribes the video with word timings. OpenAI reads the timed transcript and picks the strongest self-contained moments, each with a title, caption and hashtags."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lv-31",
      "name": "Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2700,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1180,
        "height": 460,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "### 3. Cut every clip\nOne Rendley agent run per moment: cut to the moment, reframe to 9:16 with subject tracking, remove filler words, add word-by-word captions. The loop checks the jobs every minute."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lv-32",
      "name": "Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3900,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 960,
        "height": 580,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "### 4. Export and post\nEach clip is exported in 1080p and posted to your accounts on the schedule from **Settings**. Until then it sits in the Rendley content calendar, where you can edit, reschedule or cancel it."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lv-33",
